# Open sandbox to the fixed feature (mandatory handoff)

When you finish a **user-facing** change (UI, route, portal flow, public page),
the developer must be able to test it **immediately** without hunting for the URL.

## Before you say "ready" or "done" (every agent, every pane)

1. Confirm the dev server on **this pane's port** is running (`local-agent-branch.mdc`).
2. **Always** run:

```bash
npm run sandbox:open -- </route-to-the-fix>
```

This opens the developer's browser **and** writes `.proplane-review-path` so
`/promote prakrit` can reopen the same route on integration localhost.

3. Put the **full Review URL** in your reply (`Review URL: http://localhost:…`).

## Examples

| Fix | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Manager Tasks | `npm run sandbox:open -- /portal/tasks` |
| Manager inbox | `npm run sandbox:open -- /portal/communication` |
| Resident lease | `npm run sandbox:open -- /resident/lease` |
| Listing browse | `npm run sandbox:open -- /rent/browse` |

If a modal has no deep link yet, open the parent section and say which control
to click (e.g. Tasks → **Settings**).

`--print` only when the developer asked not to steal focus.

## Prakrit promote ladder

Under Prakrit's process, agents **do not** merge to `prakrit` or `main`. The
**captain** types **`/promote prakrit`** in the lane's pane to integrate
completed, validated work (runs security review + no-mistakes, opens prakrit on
the review route). See [`AGENTS-prakrit.md`](../../docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md)
§ Standing branches, lanes, and the promote ladder.

Akhil's process defaults to keeper handoff plus the Review URL. Only an explicit
Akhil ship request authorizes agents working for him to promote his keeper →
`main` → `staging` → `production`. They do not write `prakrit`, run
no-mistakes, or waive staging and production safety.

Full doc: `docs/agents/sandbox-open-review.md`.
